WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.650
- Alright, y'all, we are back

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.870
and we've got Maestro Kaiso on violin,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.720
hanging out with band, y'all.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.110
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.760
Yeah, Maestro.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.593
Our next guest, though,

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:12.240
is one of the most
prolific children's writers

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.530
of this generation.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.595
So far, his "Diary of a Wimpy
Kid," lean in for this folks,

00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:22.595
this series has sold more
than 290 million books.

00:00:22.958 --> 00:00:25.938
(audience cheers)

00:00:25.938 --> 00:00:26.880
What?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.550
And, has been turned into seven movies.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.110
I mean, it's, like, I don't know a family

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.120
that doesn't have these
books in their house.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.660
His latest book in the collection,
"No Brainer," is out now.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.564
Everybody say hello to
Jeff Kinney. (claps hands)

00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:42.300
(audience cheers)

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.240
So, there our 18 books are the original,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.228
that's the original series, right?

00:00:47.228 --> 00:00:49.254
- Yeah, that's the main series, yeah.

00:00:49.254 --> 00:00:50.528
- Yeah, we have those.

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:51.690
we were discussing, I have
all these in my house.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.800
- That's awesome.
- Yes.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.300
they're so massively popular.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.760
Like, where did this, the
origin of all of this, start?

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.770
- Well, I wanted to be
a newspaper cartoonist,

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.240
but that didn't work out for me,

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.710
so I'm.
- I'm glad it didn't.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.210
- Oh, I appreciate that.
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.580
- So, I tried for a number
of years to get syndicated.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.680
It didn't work out, nobody liked my stuff.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.790
And, I was keeping a journal
at the time, and I thought,

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:14.010
you know what, this format
of text and some pictures

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.440
is really appealing. Nobody's
ever really done this before.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.840
So, that's how I got the idea
for "Diary of a Wimpy Kid,"

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.980
and Greg Heffley.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.780
It took me eight years to put it together.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.240
And, then I found a publisher
right here in New York.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.890
- Oh my gosh. I mean, what?

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.530
The lucky publisher that
said yes to that idea.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.470
I'm, like, good lord.
So, you're Greg, right?

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.470
It's a little bit of Greg?
- Yeah, unfortunately.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.870
- [Kelly] Yeah. Not
unfortunately! So relatable.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.379
- Well, I've got more hair
than him, but he's got a,

00:01:39.379 --> 00:01:41.730
he's a complicated character.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.361
He's, kind of, a mass of
contradictions and imperfections.

00:01:44.361 --> 00:01:47.257
Just like I was as a kid,
and just like I am now.

00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:48.090
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.621
- And, everything's just
exaggerate for comic reasons.

00:01:50.621 --> 00:01:53.400
- Yeah, I mean I think a lot
of people relate to that.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.830
That's why kids like it,
too. Like, it's relatable.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.035
- [Jeff] I think so too.
- Yeah.

00:01:57.035 --> 00:01:58.980
- If you look at Greg on the
cover of the books, he's like,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.320
he looks like he's having
a hard time of things.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.153
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:03.210
- And, I think if I put
a smile on his face,

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.920
and made him look brave or strong,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.753
it wouldn't be the same book.

00:02:05.753 --> 00:02:06.780
I think you need to know

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.670
that other people are having trouble too.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.901
- Yeah, I think that
that's very comforting.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.720
So, where do you write,
where do you go to?

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.030
'cause I write songs, like,
anywhere. Where do you write?

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:15.870
- Well, believe it or not,

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.840
I actually do a lot of my
writing in the cemetery,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.720
(chuckles) which seems dark.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.553
- What?

00:02:22.553 --> 00:02:24.630
- Yeah, it seems a little
bit dark, but, yeah,

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.040
there's a picture I think.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.120
(audience laughs)

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.279
But, my kids were doing,
you know, remote schooling

00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:31.376
during the pandemic, and I
needed a quiet place to work.

00:02:31.376 --> 00:02:36.376
So, I got in my car, got a
blanket, and some Skittles,

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.975
and some Double Stuffed Oreos.

00:02:38.975 --> 00:02:40.069
- Oh my God, you're a college kid.

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:42.237
I love this right now.
That's amazing, okay.

00:02:42.237 --> 00:02:44.640
- So, my books are really
fueled on that kind of food.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.780
It's sad.
- Oh my God.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.487
That's why it's so relatable
to kids, that's amazing.

00:02:47.487 --> 00:02:49.410
So, this new book is
called "No Brainer," right?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.243
- Yeah.

00:02:50.243 --> 00:02:51.420
- So, what's different about this one?

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.380
- This one's about,

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.283
it's like a satire of the
American education system.

00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:57.276
It's about Greg's school getting shut down

00:02:57.276 --> 00:03:01.080
because they do poorly on
their standardized tests.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.380
But, then the school demands
that if they don't, you know,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.570
raise their grades with less money,

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.190
then they're going to be closed for good.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:10.059
So, that's what the book's all about.

00:03:10.059 --> 00:03:10.892
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:03:10.892 --> 00:03:11.895
- And, I also touched on
things, like, you know,

00:03:11.895 --> 00:03:14.178
school budgets, and in-school advertising,

00:03:14.178 --> 00:03:16.061
and book banning too.

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:19.380
I satirize that because of
course it's a hot topic.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.840
- Yeah. So, tell us about,
it's the "No Brainer Tour,"

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.120
right? And, it's helping
schools and libraries?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.394
- That's right. We're
helping schools, libraries,

00:03:26.394 --> 00:03:27.617
and, well, school libraries and,

00:03:27.617 --> 00:03:29.389
- [Kelly] Yeah!
- Community libraries.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:32.010
We're giving away a
hundred thousand dollars.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:32.843
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:32.843 --> 00:03:34.505
- We're doing this game show
format, which is really cool.

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:37.020
It's different than a
regular author event.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.371
And, we're rewarding librarians,
spotlighting librarians,

00:03:39.371 --> 00:03:41.099
because now, more than ever,

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:44.460
librarians need to be
cherished and uplifted.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.330
- Yeah!
(audience claps)

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.087
And, my kids, I love the library
at our school, growing up,

00:03:48.087 --> 00:03:50.220
but my kids, that's the
thing they talk about,

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.080
the little reading nooks that
they have at their school,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:52.913
they love it!

00:03:52.913 --> 00:03:53.990
It's, like, escapism for them.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.556
- It's so important
for kids of all stripes

00:03:55.556 --> 00:03:58.252
to be able to see themselves
in the pages of a book.

00:03:58.252 --> 00:03:59.085
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:03:59.085 --> 00:04:00.750
- Represented in a positive way.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.914
- Absolutely. Well, you're awesome!

00:04:01.914 --> 00:04:02.808
Thank you for being on the show.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.486
- Well, thank you very
much. I appreciate that.

00:04:04.486 --> 00:04:05.887
- Such a fan. I'm a bigger fan now.

00:04:05.887 --> 00:04:07.675
We need a quick break, everybody,

00:04:07.675 --> 00:04:09.488
but we have a nine year old here

00:04:09.488 --> 00:04:13.440
who says he is Jeff's
biggest fan. Like, biggest.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.880
He has no idea Jeff's here.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.530
So, Jeff's gonna go hide,

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.951
and come out for one giant surprise.

00:04:17.951 --> 00:04:19.615
It's gonna be really great.

00:04:19.615 --> 00:04:20.448
(audience claps)

00:04:20.448 --> 00:04:22.386
So, Jacob, thank you for being here.

00:04:22.386 --> 00:04:25.830
And, also, are you a fan
of books, you like reading?

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:26.880
- Yep.
- Yeah?

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.100
Is "Diary of a Wimpy Kid,"
one of your favorites?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.758
- Yep.
- Yep. (laughs)

00:04:31.758 --> 00:04:34.050
So why do you love these books so much?

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.435
- I like them because it's
about a middle school kid

00:04:36.435 --> 00:04:39.300
who's misunderstood by his parents.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.222
- Also, I like that the character,

00:04:41.222 --> 00:04:44.310
that the main character
Greg relates to me a lot.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.520
He's not that good at sports.
He doesn't like to sweat.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.353
(audience laughs)

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:52.080
He likes video games. He's
really good at video games.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.690
- Yeah, I love video games too.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.855
So you, do you know anything about,

00:04:55.855 --> 00:04:57.368
I think Jeff is the writer, right?

00:04:57.368 --> 00:04:58.920
Of "Diary of a Wimpy kid?"

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.590
So, do you know anything
about Jeff Kinney?

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.877
- Not much about his personal life.

00:05:02.877 --> 00:05:04.317
(audience laughs)

00:05:04.317 --> 00:05:07.053
But, I know that he is
always thinking up good ideas

00:05:07.053 --> 00:05:08.880
and putting them into writing.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.165
- Yeah, is that something that you think

00:05:10.165 --> 00:05:12.780
you'd be interested in
doing when you grow up?

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.610
- Yep. I've already made some books.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.050
Like.
- What?

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.090
- [Kid] Yeah.
- That's crazy cool.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.200
- What are they about?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.033
- Well,

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.770
one of them is called "John
versus the Glipper Glorps."

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.603
- Yes!

00:05:23.603 --> 00:05:26.010
- And, the Glipper Glorps are these aliens

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.635
who kidnapped the entire town.

00:05:27.635 --> 00:05:29.880
- [Kelly] (gasps) I
love, I would read this.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.150
- And, and, and John and his hamster

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.014
have to save the entire town.

00:05:35.014 --> 00:05:36.427
Also!
- This is a great idea!

00:05:36.427 --> 00:05:38.360
(audience cheers)

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.277
That's an awesome idea.

00:05:41.787 --> 00:05:43.980
So, you wanna be an
author when you grow up?

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.170
- Yep.
- Yep. "Yep!" I love it.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.411
Well, I have to let Jacob
in on a little secret,

00:05:48.411 --> 00:05:51.800
because we invited you here
to review "No Brainer,"

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.040
but that wasn't all.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.142
We actually have a surprise for
you. Do you want a surprise?

00:05:55.142 --> 00:05:57.190
Do you like surprises?
- Yes!

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.688
- Okay, okay. That's good.

00:05:58.688 --> 00:06:01.417
'cause it was happening regardless, Jacob.

00:06:01.417 --> 00:06:02.250
(audience laughs)

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.530
So, the creator of the "Diary
of a Wimpy Kid," series,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.720
Jeff Kinney, is here
and wants to meet you.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.340
Is that cool?
- Yep.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.896
- Look at you right now!

00:06:09.896 --> 00:06:11.382
Come on out, Jeff!

00:06:11.382 --> 00:06:13.644
(audience cheers)

00:06:13.644 --> 00:06:15.351
Come on over.

00:06:15.351 --> 00:06:17.201
- How are you doing? Good to see you.

00:06:22.531 --> 00:06:25.937
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:25.937 --> 00:06:27.360
Jacob, this is awesome.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.710
I can't believe I'm getting to meet you.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:31.380
You're like a legend,
everybody knows about Jacob.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.038
I've heard all about your
stories, and you're like an expert

00:06:34.038 --> 00:06:36.321
at "The Diary of Movie
Kid" books, aren't you?

00:06:36.321 --> 00:06:37.950
- Mhm.
- This is pretty cool.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.150
This is cool. Look at this, we're.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.486
- You completely pivoted
his entire physicality.

00:06:41.486 --> 00:06:42.836
(everyone laughs)

00:06:42.836 --> 00:06:43.890
- He's like, "I'm not sure about this."

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:46.039
- He said, "And, who's she?" And then.

00:06:46.039 --> 00:06:48.926
I love it. No, stay there!
I love it, I love it.

00:06:48.926 --> 00:06:51.150
Is that a good surprise?
- Yep!

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.250
- Yeah, yeah? (laughs and claps)

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.619
So, Jeff, do you want to
say anything to Jacob?

00:06:55.619 --> 00:06:57.925
- Yeah, first of all,
thank you for being a fan,

00:06:57.925 --> 00:07:00.660
but I also wanted to say I have a studio

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.910
in Plainville, Massachusetts,
in my bookstore,

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.990
on the top floor.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.670
It's really cool, it's really colorful.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.830
It's like the center
of the Wimpy Kid world.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.845
And, I would like to invite
you and your family up

00:07:10.845 --> 00:07:15.510
to spend time with me in the
studio, draw on my computer,

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.120
and we'll have some pizza,
and talk about books,

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.080
and talk about your books.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.970
Is that sound like a good idea?

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.449
- Yep.
- All right.

00:07:22.449 --> 00:07:24.685
(all clap)

00:07:24.685 --> 00:07:26.654
Great, all right, let's seal on the deal.

00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:28.987
- Oh my god, I love you two!

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:31.904
Y'all should do something together.

00:07:31.904 --> 00:07:33.646
Well, we need a break.

00:07:33.646 --> 00:07:35.910
I don't want a break,
'cause it's so special.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.227
But, pick up Jeff's
latest book, everybody,

00:07:38.227 --> 00:07:40.110
"Diary of a Wimpy Kid, No Brainer."

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:44.066
It's out now, and everyone
here is going home with a copy.

00:07:44.066 --> 00:07:46.222
(audience cheers)

